182	 * against it would be thrown away.
183	 *
184	 * `needsCiDispatch` is the recovery path for a required check that never got
185	 * written -- the normal path is `create_pr` and `commit_and_push` dispatching
186	 * validation, and this exists for when that did not happen. It fires when a
187	 * check is missing and nothing in this list is in the way.
188	 *
189	 * It used to fire only when `checks-missing` was the sole blocker, which is a
190	 * different and much narrower rule: `merge.policy` defaults to `"manual"`, and
191	 * that adds a `merge-policy` blocker to every pull request. So on any project
192	 * using the default -- most of them -- the recovery path could never run at all,
193	 * and the person who has to do the merge was left waiting on a required check
194	 * that nothing was going to create.
195	 *
196	 * The rule is now about the commit rather than about the merge. `merge-policy`,
197	 * `human-authored`, `governance-change`, `merge-gate`, `gate-config-invalid`,
198	 * `governance-unknown` and `blocked` all stop the agent from merging and leave
199	 * the head commit exactly as it is -- so the check is still needed, and still
200	 * worth writing, by whoever ends up merging. The kinds below are the ones where
201	 * it is not: the commit must change first, or there is nothing to validate.
